 {:seon.task/name "every-tools-answer-says-what-it-is"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-11-11: 'Agents need to know that context exists and we need explanations and short instructions that the agent can use to pull in more context'; and on the default printer: '(+ 1 1) ... I want the answer'. What exists, counted: about 55 public tools in my.agent and my.db; four answer a value whose metadata names a schema that declares a model render (the lines of a file, a search that found nothing, a proved test, a merged branch: docs/render.md#how-a-value-is-printed); the rest answer plain values the printer cuts with no word of what was cut or how to get it. Plan: one way. Each tool's answer carries the schema that names it, and that schema's entry holds its description, its model render and what brings more; a plain value from the agent's own form prints plainly, as now. No tool formats a string of its own. Deletes: each tool's own formatting as it is moved. Proof, red first: a law over every public var of the tool namespaces: its contract's answer is a registered schema with a description, or the var is a plain function of values named as such by its metadata; the count of tools outside the law may only fall."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.main-test/every-tools-answer-says-what-it-is}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-process-holds-mains-source-roots-from-its-start"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: runtime (the loader and a process's start). Root's review of dd6c0301a3 (2026-11-15): seon.program/required! appends the source dirs of the tree main was imported from to this process's source roots (jolt.host/set-source-roots!) before it requires a test namespace whole: a process-global write in the loader, made in a function that reads, so a prove agent in the image finds the file it found (tests' fix for seon.source-test/a-test-namespace-loads-whole-from-the-tree-main-was-imported-from). The write's owner is a process's start: seon.main/checkout-roots! already puts a checkout's test/ and src/ on the roots for the processes that call it, and the image's processes (root's fork server, an agent, a test child) do not. Move it there: every process that loads main's program holds main's source dirs (its :seon.system/source root) on its roots from its start, and required! only reads them (its write deleted). Proof: the same test, which takes test/ off its process's roots, green with required! reading only."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.source-test/a-test-namespace-loads-whole-from-the-tree-main-was-imported-from}
  :seon.task/estimate #:seon.main{checkout-roots! {:n 1, :order :constant, :ticks 100000, :bytes 100000}}
  :seon.task/needs #{}}
